[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" "question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" "question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" "question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" "question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119536 :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n1, \\: 4, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}1},$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 4 1 = {\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = {\\color{red}4} \\cdot a_{n} , \\qquad a_1 = {\\color{blue}1}, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119537 :question/problem "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -3 a_n,\\qquad a_1 = 2,\\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-3{a}_{1}=-3(2)=-6 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-3{a}_{2}=-3(-6)=18 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-3{a}_{3}=-3(18)=-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_4 = -54.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119584 :question/problem "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = -5f(n),\\quad f(1) = -1,\\quad  n\\geq 1\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-1 \\\\ f(2) & =-5f(1)=-5(-1)=5 \\\\ f(3) & =-5f(2)=-5(5)=-25 \\\\ f(4) & =-5f(3)=-5(-25)=125 \\\\ f(5) & =-5f(4)=-5(125)=-625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(5)=-625.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119538 :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\nI. $10, \\: 20, \\: 30, \\: 40, \\: \\dots$\n\nII. $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n,\\quad a_1 = 36,\\quad n\\geq 1$\n\nIII. $f(n+1) = 2f(n)-1,\\quad f(1) =2,\\quad  n\\geq 1$" :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence I is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{20}{10} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{30}{20} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Sequence II is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n$ tells us that each term is $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=\\dfrac{1}{6}.$\n\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =2 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot f(1)-1=2\\cdot 2-1=3 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot f(2)-1=2\\cdot 3-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/id #uuid "225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-249796" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n-48,\\,36,\\,-27,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-48,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{36}{-48}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-48,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" "answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/id #uuid "6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/id #uuid "2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/id #uuid "6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109804" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n3,\\,-12,\\,48,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=3,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{3}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" "answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" "answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" "answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" "answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/id #uuid "a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/id #uuid "5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/id #uuid "cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/id #uuid "f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-4,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/id #uuid "59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-4,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/id #uuid "a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/math-academy-id "q-249793" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n64,\\,32,\\,16,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{32}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=64,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" "answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/id #uuid "7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/id #uuid "e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a_n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer-field/choices ["answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/id #uuid "530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/id #uuid "5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109803" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n5,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=5,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/id #uuid "256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" "answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" "answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" "answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" "answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/id #uuid "e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=5{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/id #uuid "6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/id #uuid "5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/id #uuid "6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/id #uuid "5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+\\frac{1}{5},\\,{a}_{1}=1,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/id #uuid "498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44900" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n24,\\,-12,\\,6,\\,…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=24,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{24}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" "answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" "answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" "answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" "answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/id #uuid "786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/id #uuid "0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{2}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/id #uuid "eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/id #uuid "6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/id #uuid "198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-36,\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120994 :tutorial/content "The common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) of a geometric sequence is found by dividing any term by the term immediately before it:\n![](images/64/641727086c22a06619c11617fae703a715530b8436e05ea22ad57cfffdbf9e8f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the **recursive formula for a geometric sequence** with common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) takes the form\n![](images/c6/c68961a8641390e8d86b86ec557512300a53f424912bed25e9939126e5d71c07.svg)\n\nThe above formula states that to get to the next term in the sequence, we multiply the previous term by ![](images/b2/b2e0c6bf822f391aab6c59cc540176f139c5c69f5a6f54ae9c81d451defe9c9f.svg)\n\nTo illustrate, consider the geometric sequence below:\n\n![](images/7c/7ceb288dea6b0c885bae7014d7170c923afb2d38b8ba6cb338cd63c32e6af5c0.svg)\n\nThe first term is ![](images/82/82447c5e47fb052201522cca2359b821307def74212b7ce26debbfd8875f4dc2.svg) and we can calculate the common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) as\n\n![](images/d2/d2c615fcab22a64d8f610b7ff36d28190b787c456e9e4099d8f5be2522dafd9c.svg)\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n![](images/9d/9d7aaea9acc235b192240da83d3e53d9d62ee6e67e128df01dba6bd0d1ced4ad.svg)\n\nWhen writing out our final answer for the recursive formula, we should also state the first term and the range for ![](images/c2/c2475d72e6ec36042292de6c0160930174172b2386148d823a70e59fddfb93c2.svg)\n\nTo check that the recursive formula is correct, we can use it to generate the next few terms of the series:\n\n![](images/b3/b397de9b364d11653d651b7fa2d6ddf422ede5fca1692596f527e3e293bafb27.svg)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120025 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186119536 :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n1, \\: 4, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots\n$$"] [17592186119536 :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is $a_1={\\color{blue}1},$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 4 1 = {\\color{red}4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = {\\color{red}4} \\cdot a_{n} , \\qquad a_1 = {\\color{blue}1}, \\qquad n\\geq 1.\n$$"] [17592186119537 :question/problem "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = -3 a_n,\\qquad a_1 = 2,\\qquad n \\geq 1\n$$"] [17592186119537 :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-3{a}_{1}=-3(2)=-6 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-3{a}_{2}=-3(-6)=18 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =-3{a}_{3}=-3(18)=-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_4 = -54.$"] [17592186119584 :question/problem "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1) = -5f(n),\\quad f(1) = -1,\\quad  n\\geq 1\n$$"] [17592186119584 :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =-1 \\\\ f(2) & =-5f(1)=-5(-1)=5 \\\\ f(3) & =-5f(2)=-5(5)=-25 \\\\ f(4) & =-5f(3)=-5(-25)=125 \\\\ f(5) & =-5f(4)=-5(125)=-625\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(5)=-625.$"] [17592186119538 :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\nI. $10, \\: 20, \\: 30, \\: 40, \\: \\dots$\n\nII. $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n,\\quad a_1 = 36,\\quad n\\geq 1$\n\nIII. $f(n+1) = 2f(n)-1,\\quad f(1) =2,\\quad  n\\geq 1$"] [17592186119538 :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence I is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{20}{10} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{3}}{{a}_{2}}=\\frac{30}{20} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Sequence II is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n$ tells us that each term is $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=\\dfrac{1}{6}.$\n\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =2 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot f(1)-1=2\\cdot 2-1=3 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot f(2)-1=2\\cdot 3-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence."] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/id #uuid "225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/math-academy-id "q-249796"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n-48,\\,36,\\,-27,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=-48,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{36}{-48}=-\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-48,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/id #uuid "a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8"] ["answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/id #uuid "6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a"] ["answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a" :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}{a}_{n}"] ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/correct "answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a"] ["answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8" :answer-field/choices "answer-6dc75461-f680-52f9-bdb9-64d7afe41e1a"] ["answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6"] ["answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/id #uuid "2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9"] ["answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9" :answer/value "-48"] ["answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/correct "answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9"] ["answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6" :answer-field/choices "answer-2acc437e-a412-581d-8e81-dfe5cfc62ad9"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-a57da2c0-90ed-5f07-addb-e7aacf7566d8"] ["question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-9f053b0a-afab-5b22-80de-3501f84a15e6"] [17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions "question-225e6266-f488-590a-bcc1-b7110b1ab57c"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/id #uuid "6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/math-academy-id "q-109804"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n3,\\,-12,\\,48,\\,…\n$$"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=3,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{3}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7"] ["answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/id #uuid "a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa"] ["answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/id #uuid "5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81"] ["answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/id #uuid "cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0"] ["answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=3,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/id #uuid "f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be"] ["answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-4,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/id #uuid "59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252"] ["answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-4,\\,{a}_{1}=7,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/correct "answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/choices "answer-a09ab400-53e2-5d77-99dd-4639394319aa"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/choices "answer-5e627b36-0bed-53c2-87b0-11792e481c81"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/choices "answer-cb91e927-0186-52d3-b60a-f7d417fe23d0"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/choices "answer-f2a7e502-4c1c-5f69-ba12-c209563b85be"] ["answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7" :answer-field/choices "answer-59109616-a72d-56f4-b284-2356b9a3a252"] ["question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7d7dfc4c-3be2-5c52-8f14-4925b82dc4d7"] [17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions "question-6e05b66e-ca2b-55a8-b1d5-5df4f7e7120d"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/id #uuid "a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/math-academy-id "q-249793"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n64,\\,32,\\,16,\\,…\n$$\n\nThe recursive formula for this geometric sequence is\n\n${a}_{n+1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{a}_{1}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,n\\ge 1.$"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=64,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{32}{64}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=64,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/id #uuid "7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74"] ["answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/id #uuid "e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70"] ["answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}a_n"] ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/correct "answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70"] ["answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74" :answer-field/choices "answer-e39963bd-2dfe-5a7e-adaa-2c2cf677ac70"] ["answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96"] ["answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/id #uuid "530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70"] ["answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70" :answer/value "64"] ["answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/correct "answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70"] ["answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96" :answer-field/choices "answer-530993ed-b33b-597f-ad91-770ac1be6f70"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7685adc9-c06d-5b60-9d9b-882b9ed5af74"] ["question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c9ff6506-1647-592e-b5f6-dfcf283ece96"] [17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a5329a3e-b8b4-504e-8c17-47d6c0564352"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/id #uuid "5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-109803"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n5,\\,1,\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,…\n$$"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=5,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/id #uuid "256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2"] ["answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/id #uuid "e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4"] ["answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=5{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/id #uuid "6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3"] ["answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=2,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/id #uuid "5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5"] ["answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{5}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/id #uuid "6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2"] ["answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+5,\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/id #uuid "5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984"] ["answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}+\\frac{1}{5},\\,{a}_{1}=1,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/correct "answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/choices "answer-e1e388cb-bd96-503a-915d-cbba5975a2c4"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/choices "answer-6ed046c8-7602-5017-b313-39c70d6930b3"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/choices "answer-5a6271c4-dc33-5178-8880-d84db8f789e5"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/choices "answer-6b8951a6-e073-51d8-932a-75d271fd5be2"] ["answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2" :answer-field/choices "answer-5fd17d56-55b0-5789-8b8e-7b8949679984"] ["question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-256ce9ac-b6f2-58d9-9923-d36fccd40be2"] [17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5f82136c-d352-5849-8678-e3857b7e43c6"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/id #uuid "498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-44900"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n\n$$\n24,\\,-12,\\,6,\\,…\n$$"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is ${a}_{1}=24,$ and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-12}{24}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1.\n$$"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3"] ["answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/id #uuid "786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748"] ["answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/id #uuid "0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a"] ["answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{2}=24,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/id #uuid "eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9"] ["answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/id #uuid "6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3"] ["answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/id #uuid "198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed"] ["answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed" :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-36,\\,{a}_{1}=24,\\,n\\ge 1"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/correct "answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/choices "answer-786b34ba-15b9-5365-b95c-9713f3204748"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/choices "answer-0d07ba6b-560e-5f76-bba4-ab3cc421726a"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/choices "answer-eabbcd8b-e3e1-568e-8bb4-7faa54e7eac9"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/choices "answer-6f636481-d088-57f3-b4e1-1fff7ed219c3"] ["answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3" :answer-field/choices "answer-198dd29e-d1f9-5b83-b5d6-a3755e2179ed"] ["question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e6960de4-32f2-5e23-a67e-c1fd22c3c7b3"] [17592186119950 :knowledge-point/questions "question-498cc30d-95e0-5d5e-8baf-d608afabcdc8"] [17592186120994 :tutorial/content "The common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) of a geometric sequence is found by dividing any term by the term immediately before it:\n![](images/64/641727086c22a06619c11617fae703a715530b8436e05ea22ad57cfffdbf9e8f.svg)\n\nTherefore, the **recursive formula for a geometric sequence** with common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) takes the form\n![](images/c6/c68961a8641390e8d86b86ec557512300a53f424912bed25e9939126e5d71c07.svg)\n\nThe above formula states that to get to the next term in the sequence, we multiply the previous term by ![](images/b2/b2e0c6bf822f391aab6c59cc540176f139c5c69f5a6f54ae9c81d451defe9c9f.svg)\n\nTo illustrate, consider the geometric sequence below:\n\n![](images/7c/7ceb288dea6b0c885bae7014d7170c923afb2d38b8ba6cb338cd63c32e6af5c0.svg)\n\nThe first term is ![](images/82/82447c5e47fb052201522cca2359b821307def74212b7ce26debbfd8875f4dc2.svg) and we can calculate the common ratio ![](images/3a/3a4ef1c1b261a53f9c45d0c90f2d44b155125fe1e7b1359406830111b4846f2f.svg) as\n\n![](images/d2/d2c615fcab22a64d8f610b7ff36d28190b787c456e9e4099d8f5be2522dafd9c.svg)\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n![](images/9d/9d7aaea9acc235b192240da83d3e53d9d62ee6e67e128df01dba6bd0d1ced4ad.svg)\n\nWhen writing out our final answer for the recursive formula, we should also state the first term and the range for ![](images/c2/c2475d72e6ec36042292de6c0160930174172b2386148d823a70e59fddfb93c2.svg)\n\nTo check that the recursive formula is correct, we can use it to generate the next few terms of the series:\n\n![](images/b3/b397de9b364d11653d651b7fa2d6ddf422ede5fca1692596f527e3e293bafb27.svg)"] [17592186120025 :activity/expected-seconds 540.0]] "retractions" [[17592186119536 :question/problem "What is the recursive formula for the following geometric sequence?\n$1, \\: 4, \\: 16, \\: \\ldots$"] [17592186119536 :question/worked-solution "The recursive formula for a geometric sequence with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the first term is\n\n$$\na_1={\\color{blue}1}\n$$\n\nand we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 4 1 = {\\color{red}4}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = {\\color{red}4} \\cdot a_{n}, \\qquad a_1 = {\\color{blue}1}, \\qquad n\\geq 1\n$$"] [17592186119537 :question/problem "What is the $4$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n$a_{n+1} = -3 a_n,\\qquad a_1 = 2,\\qquad n \\geq 1$"] [17592186119537 :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{1} &= 2 \\\\\na_{2} &= -3a_{1} =-3(2) =-6 \\\\\na_{3} &= -3a_{2} =-3(-6) = 18 \\\\\na_{4} &= -3a_{3} =-3(18) =-54\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a_4 = -54$."] [17592186119584 :question/problem "What is the $5$th term of the geometric sequence given below?\n\n$f(n+1) = -5f(n),\\quad f(1) = -1,\\quad n\\geq 1$"] [17592186119584 :question/worked-solution "We use the recursive formula to compute the terms of the sequence up to the $4$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= -1 \\\\\nf(2) &= -5f(1) =-5(-1) = 5 \\\\\nf(3) &= -5f(2) =-5(5) =-25 \\\\\nf(4) &= -5f(3) =-5(-25) = 125 \\\\\nf(5) &= -5f(4) =-5(125) =-625\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(5)=-625\n$$"] [17592186119538 :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\n1. $10, \\: 20, \\: 30, \\: 40, \\: \\dots$\n2. $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n,\\quad a_1 = 36,\\quad n\\geq 1$\n3. $f(n+1) = 2f(n)-1,\\quad f(1) =2,\\quad n\\geq 1$"] [17592186119538 :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence I is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n$\\frac{a_{2}}{a_{1}} = \\frac{20}{10}|= 2; \\frac{a_{3}}{a_{2}} = \\frac{30}{20}|= \\frac{3}{2}$\n- Sequence II is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule $a_{n+1} = \\dfrac{1}{6}a_n$ tells us that each term is $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=\\dfrac{1}{6}$.\n- Sequence III is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms.\n$f(1)|= 2; f(2)|= 2 \\cdot f(1) - 1 = 2 \\cdot 2 - 1 = 3; f(3)|= 2 \\cdot f(2) - 1 = 2 \\cdot 3 - 1 = 5$\nThe first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n$(f(2))/(f(1)) = \\frac{3}{2}; (f(3))/(f(2)) = \\frac{5}{3}$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence II is a geometric sequence."] [17592186120994 :tutorial/content "The **recursive formula for a geometric sequence** with common ratio $r$ takes the form\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = r \\cdot a_{n}\n$$\n\nThe above formula states that to get to the next term in the sequence, we multiply the previous term by $r$.\n\nTo illustrate, consider the geometric sequence below:\n\n$$\n1, \\: 3, \\: 9, \\: 27, \\: \\dots\n$$\n\nThe first term is $a_1=1$, and we can calculate the common ratio $r$ as\n\n$$\nr = \\dfrac{a_2}{a_1} = \\dfrac 3 1 = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the recursive formula is\n\n$$\na_{n+1} = 3 \\cdot a_{n}, \\qquad a_1 = 1, \\qquad n\\geq 1\n$$\n\nWhen writing out our final answer for the recursive formula, we should also state the first term and the range for $n$.\n\nTo check that the recursive formula is correct, we can use it to generate the next few terms of the series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{2} &= 3 \\cdot a_{1} = 3 \\cdot 1 = 30✓ \\\\\na_{3} &= 3 \\cdot a_{2} = 3 \\cdot 3 = 90✓ \\\\\na_{4} &= 3 \\cdot a_{3} = 3 \\cdot 9 = 27✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]]}]